## Test the v09 -> v08 conversion of meta data that tracks more than 4k of data
## per bitmap bit.
##
## Bug guarded against: md_convert_09_to_08() carried bm_bytes_per_bit over from
## the v09 meta data.  DRBD 8.4 compares that field against its compile-time
## BM_BLOCK_SIZE and refuses to attach ("unexpected bm_bytes_per_bit: 8192
## (expected 4096)"), while drbdmeta kept reporting the very same block as valid.
##
## Test layout: 256 MB image, flex-internal meta data, one peer, 8k per bitmap
## bit.  The 4k bitmap of the converted meta data needs 8 sectors more, so
## md_size_sect grows from 80 to 88 and the data area shrinks accordingly.
##
## When re-initializing bitmaps, drbdmeta tries ioctl BLKZEROOUT first,
## which is expected to fail in these tests using tmpfiles,
## then falls back to pwrite.
##
## The test walks through, in this order:
##  - an in-sync device converts, and gets a bitmap of the 4k granularity
##  - bits set in the old bitmap describe other blocks than the new bits do, so
##    they can not be carried over: everything is marked out-of-sync instead
##  - the same, with 3 peers, where a bit set in the last third of the bitmap is
##    only found when looking at the bitmap before dropping the peer slots
##  - if the last agreed device size leaves no room for the larger bitmap, the
##    conversion is refused, and the v09 meta data stays as it is.
##    524208 sectors is all a 256 MB image leaves with the 8k bitmap
##  - the same, with a last agreed device size that is not a whole kB: sizes and
##    the difference are then reported in sectors, or a difference of a single
##    sector would print as no difference at all
##  - the 4k granularity with more than one peer slot also needs a new bitmap:
##    dropping the peer slots moves the bitmap area, and the bits of the
##    interleaved slots do not line up with the bits of the single v08 slot
##  - meta data of the 4k granularity with one peer converts without touching
##    the bitmap
##  - --initialize-bitmap overrides what the conversion decides on its own:
##    set-all on an in-sync device, and a zeroing variant on a device that has
##    out-of-sync bits.  With skip it also says that the bitmap area is left
##    holding bits that describe other blocks now
##  - external meta data, where the bitmap is the last thing in the meta data
##    area rather than being followed by the activity log: a last agreed device
##    size that the bitmap area can not cover at all must not make the scan read
##    past the end of the device.  32 MB of external meta data track 2 TB with
##    8k per bitmap bit, the size used below asks for 2.3 TB.

$ tmpdir=$(mktemp -d) && img=$(mktemp --suffix=.img)
$ truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K 1 2>/dev/null
initializing activity log
Writing meta data...
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -c '[.bm_bytes_per_bit, .md_size_sect]'
[8192,80]
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^Bitmap block size' -e '^re-creating' -e '^initializing the new bitmap'
Bitmap block size 8192 is not supported by DRBD 8.4 and older,
re-creating the bitmap with 4096 bytes per bit.
initializing the new bitmap (8 KB) to all zero
initializing the new bitmap (8 KB) to all zero using pwrite
$ drbdmeta --force - v08 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -c '[.bm_bytes_per_bit, .md_size_sect, .["#meta"].valid]'
[4096,88,"VALID_MD_FOUND"]
$ bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v08 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ od -An -j "$bm_abs" -N 8 -tx1 "$img"
 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --effective-size 100000 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ old_bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ printf '\001' | dd of="$img" bs=1 seek="$old_bm_abs" count=1 conv=notrunc status=none
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^marking the whole device'
marking the whole device out-of-sync in the new bitmap (8 KB)
$ bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v08 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ od -An -j "$bm_abs" -N 8 -tx1 "$img"
 ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --effective-size 524192 3 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ old_bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ printf '\001' | dd of="$img" bs=1 seek=$((old_bm_abs + 8000)) count=1 conv=notrunc status=none
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^marking the whole device'
marking the whole device out-of-sync in the new bitmap (8 KB)
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --effective-size 524208 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^The 4096 byte bitmap' -e '^while the last' -e '^DRBD 8.4 would' -e '^Shrink' -e '^Conversion refused'; echo "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
The 4096 byte bitmap leaves only 262100 kB of this device usable,
while the last agreed device size is 262104 kB.
DRBD 8.4 would refuse to attach that, or truncate the device.
Shrink the file system and the DRBD device by 4 kB or more
Conversion refused.
10
$ drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -c '[.bm_bytes_per_bit, .md_size_sect, .effective_size, .["#meta"].valid]'
[8192,80,524208,"VALID_MD_FOUND"]
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --effective-size 524201 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^The 4096 byte bitmap' -e '^while the last' -e '^Shrink'
The 4096 byte bitmap leaves only 524200 sectors of this device usable,
while the last agreed device size is 524201 sectors.
Shrink the file system and the DRBD device by 1 sector or more
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md --effective-size 500000 3 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ old_bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ printf '\001' | dd of="$img" bs=1 seek="$old_bm_abs" count=1 conv=notrunc status=none
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^Bitmap slots' -e '^marking the whole device'
Bitmap slots for 3 peers are not supported by DRBD 8.4 and older,
marking the whole device out-of-sync in the new bitmap (8 KB)
$ bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v08 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ od -An -j "$bm_abs" -N 8 -tx1 "$img"
 ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e bitmap; echo "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
0
$ drbdmeta --force - v08 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -c '[.bm_bytes_per_bit, .["#meta"].valid]'
[4096,"VALID_MD_FOUND"]
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 268435456 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-internal create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --effective-size 100000 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ cp "$img" "$tmpdir/clean.img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md --initialize-bitmap set-all 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^initializing' -e '^marking'
marking the whole device out-of-sync in the new bitmap (8 KB)
$ bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v08 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ od -An -j "$bm_abs" -N 8 -tx1 "$img"
 ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
$ cp "$tmpdir/clean.img" "$img"
$ old_bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v09 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ printf '\001' | dd of="$img" bs=1 seek="$old_bm_abs" count=1 conv=notrunc status=none
$ cp "$img" "$tmpdir/dirty.img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md --initialize-bitmap pwrite 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^initializing' -e '^marking'
initializing the new bitmap (8 KB) to all zero using pwrite
$ bm_abs=$(drbdmeta --force - v08 "$img" flex-internal dump-superblock --output json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '(.["#meta"].dump_offset + .bm_offset * 512)')
$ od -An -j "$bm_abs" -N 8 -tx1 "$img"
 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
$ cp "$tmpdir/dirty.img" "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-internal create-md --initialize-bitmap skip 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^skipping' -e '^geometry changed' -e '^SKIPPED'
skipping the bitmap initialization even though the bitmap
geometry changed: the bitmap area holds stale bits now
SKIPPED initializing the new bitmap area
$ rm -f "$img" && truncate -s 33554432 "$img"
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v09 "$img" flex-external create-md --bitmap-block-size 8K --effective-size 5000000000 1 2>/dev/null | tail -1
New drbd meta data block successfully created.
$ drbdmeta --force --var-lib-drbd "$tmpdir" - v08 "$img" flex-external create-md 2>&1 >/dev/null | grep -e '^confused' -e '^Conversion refused'; echo "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
Conversion refused.
10
$ rm -rf "$tmpdir" "$img"
